This product includes software derived from OWASP ZAP and its add-ons
(https://github.com/zaproxy/zaproxy, https://github.com/zaproxy/zap-extensions),
Copyright the ZAP development team, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
- crates/core/src/scan/passive/rules/: passive scan rules ported from the pscanrules
  add-on, including their alert texts. Each file names the ZAP class it was ported from.
- crates/core/src/scan/passive/data/: data files copied from the pscanrules add-on.
- crates/core/src/scan/active/rules/: active scan rules ported from the ascanrules and
  ascanrulesBeta add-ons and helpers from the commonlib add-on (AbstractAppFilePlugin, ComparableResponse,
  TimingUtils), including their alert texts and payload lists.
- crates/core/src/scan/active/rules/probes/data/hidden_files.json: copied from ascanrules.
- crates/core/src/scan/passive/rules/content/vulnerable_js.rs: ported from the retire add-on.
- feed/passive/php/: checks generated (scripts/php_feed.py) from the pscanrules add-on's
  php-known-vulnerabilities.json, covering its ServerSideVersionScanRule.

The vulnerable JavaScript library database (crates/core/src/scan/passive/data/jsrepository.json,
as the ZAP retire add-on ships it) is from Retire.js (https://github.com/RetireJS/retire.js),
Copyright the Retire.js authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

